The plan for this session is written: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The planned commit didn't happen because .gitignore excludes session_plan/, so git refused to add it. The harness template's || true covers that failure.

Task 1: `Fixes #1010` (product, safety). Today the deny list only matches the command as it is spelled, so X=rm; $X -rf ~ gets past it.
• The deny list will check each part of a compound command separately, ignoring leading VAR=value, export and declare prefixes.
• When a deny list is set, a command whose program name comes from $VAR, $(...) or backticks is refused.
• Users with no deny list see exactly the same behaviour as before, and there is a test pinning that.
• The trade #1010 left open is decided here: with a deny list set, "$CARGO" build is refused, and a test records the reasoning.
• The docs sentence in permissions.md that promises spelling-only matching gets rewritten.
• The `eval "$(...)" gap gets its own new issue, so Fixes #1010` doesn't quietly close it.

Task 2: `Part of #1004` (evolve). The price audit currently files a wrong nonzero cache-read price as harmless. Sonnet 5.5 is listed at 0.2 against a catalogue price of 0.1, and the alarm stays silent.
• The fix adds the missing == 0.0 check, with a test that must still pass for the harmless case.
• The per-row column will use the same classification as the summary, so the two lines stop disagreeing.
• The Sonnet 5.5 price only changes if Anthropic's own pricing or yoagent's bundled table can actually be read. Otherwise the result is written up as "price unverified", not "already correct".

